{
  "name": "annas_hummingbird",
  "version": 1,
  "introduced_by": "ribshore",
  "notes": "hum: Anna's hummingbird, a male: bronze-green back, grey belly, and a gorget and crown of rose-magenta that look near black until the sun catches them, when they flash (the gorget's fourth colour value below zero is iridescence, scene.wgsl). Sits on a bare twig at the top of a shrub, darts out to hover at flowers -- lupine, ocotillo in spring, desert willow, meadow wildflowers -- and now and then climbs high and dives in a narrow U, again and again, the way it courts. Year round on the Pacific coast and in the desert. The base of the hummingbirds. Drawn on 5 mm voxels, about half again life size, so it shows.",
